            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Milton D. Miller II",
                        "email": "mdmii@outlook.com",
                        "username": "mdmillerii"
                    },
                    "message": "these are all valid reasons for wanting to change.  \n\nhowever I'd like some discussion on what happens when we want to change the list of services under management on a code update."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "If no persistent file is found for a monitored service then the default will be whatever systemd says it is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 281,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Milton D. Miller II",
                        "email": "mdmii@outlook.com",
                        "username": "mdmillerii"
                    },
                    "message": "wait you are loading the state after registering the interface for response?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 281,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Sort of? Within this function we query systemd for the actual state of the services and sockets. We put that on d-bus, and then immediately after we query what the values should be based on the persistent settings. We then correct systemd if they mismatch. If a correction is needed then this service will reject any dbus requests until that has completed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 281,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 329,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Wrap this around the compile flag"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 334,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Check for errors on file load and parsing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/srvcfg_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 335,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Per previous review comment, utilize nlohmann instead of cereal"
                }
